@* The list is a [popover], so it sits in the top layer: no z-index to lose, no clipping by an
   ancestor's overflow, and Escape closes it because the platform says so. Which is why this one
   works inside a scrolling card, where a positioned div would be cut off. *@
<Card Class="h-40 w-96 overflow-y-auto">
    <CardContent Class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">A short, scrolling card.</p>
        <Combobox Target="cb-popup-list">
            <input type="hidden" name="country" value="vn" data-combobox-value />
            <ComboboxTrigger id="cb-popup" Target="cb-popup-list">
                <ComboboxValue data-placeholder="Choose a country…">Việt Nam</ComboboxValue>
            </ComboboxTrigger>
            <ComboboxContent Id="cb-popup-list" Class="w-72">
                <ComboboxList>
                    <ComboboxEmpty>No country by that name.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="vn" Selected>Việt Nam</ComboboxItem>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="de">Deutschland</ComboboxItem>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="pt">Portugal</ComboboxItem>
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxContent>
        </Combobox>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Open it: the list escapes this box.</p>
    </CardContent>
</Card>
